      "message": "fix(wire): accept the facet mitre of a meshed round in the corner check\n\nThe wire cover law read the profile's mesh chords. An r0.25 fillet in\nfour 22.5 degree chords left the polygon offset 3.2 um past the kerf\noffset at each facet vertex, over COVER_TOL, so a legal radius was\nrefused. rounds.rs now finds facet vertices of a meshed round (turn of\n30 degrees or less, a circle of radius >= the offset and chord sag of\n0.02 mm or less, shared with a neighbour) and the cover law allows their\nexact mitre excess. Sharp corners, lone kinks, drawn polygons and radii\nunder the minimum stay refused.\n\nFixes #3208\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
